{"results": [{"id": "FAM:SF-APPM-039", "score": 0.114, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPM-039 | Study family SF-APPM-039: Travel x fit screen and outcome holdout validation\n- observed_research_question: Travel x fit screen and outcome holdout validation\n- auto_outcome_status: supported\n- observed_hypothesis: Forecast portability (travel) and fit quadrants predict mover outcomes (embedded minutes, net rating).\n- observed_result: LOO corr 0.1998, AUC 0.5986; holdout additive embedded 89.59% vs irrelevant 48.11%; P(add emb > irr)=0.984; P(add net > irr)=0.99; corr(travel,net) 0.1881.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: D_positive (no failure: positive result)\n- observed_failure_evidence: Additive > irrelevant in 98.4% of splits.\n- observed_sample_and_power: n=230\n- auto_validation_status: same_pipeline_validation; evidence: APPM-039: 'utcomes); loo travel forecast; 500 random 50/50 calibration/holdout splits. loo corr 0.1998, auc 0.5986; holdout additive embed'\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-PAP-033\n- observed_method: 296 movers (230 with outcomes); LOO travel forecast; 500 random 50/50 calibration/holdout splits."}, {"id": "FAM:SF-PAP-033", "score": 0.105, "document": "# FAM:SF-PAP-033 | Study family SF-PAP-033: Split-half validation of travel x fit outcome ordering\n- observed_research_question: Split-half validation of travel x fit outcome ordering\n- auto_outcome_status: supported\n- observed_hypothesis: Additive > irrelevant on destination embedded minutes and on-court net rating survives when travel OLS and medians are fit on a calibration half and scored on holdout.\n- observed_result: 500 splits; embedded-rate gap median=+0.116 [10-90% -0.033, +0.248] P(>0)=0.838; net-rtg gap median=+2.926 [+0.541, +5.072] P(>0)=0.960; corr(travel forecast, net rtg) median=+0.178 P(>0)=0.976; corr(delta, net) median=+ [cut; read_family for the full text]\n- auto_failure_mechanism: D_positive (no failure: positive result)\n- observed_failure_evidence: additive>irrelevant on net rating in 96% of holdout splits; minutes gap positive in 84%\n- observed_sample_and_power: n~198 movers, 500 splits, half~99\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-APPM-039\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF-PAP-032\n- observed_verdict: supported"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-052", "score": 0.092, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPA-052 | Study family SF-APPA-052: CUT feasibility cap: BEST-AVOID gap without CUT-heavy games\n- observed_research_question: CUT feasibility cap: BEST-AVOID gap without CUT-heavy games\n- auto_outcome_status: supported\n- observed_hypothesis: The BEST vs AVOID gap is inflated by games where CUT exceeds 15% of H2 mix.\n- observed_result: All games BEST 1.473 vs AVOID 0.853 gap +0.620 MW p=0.0000 Spearman -0.316 n=2,544. CUT<=15%: +0.625 n=2,508. CUT>15%: +0.163 n.s. n=36. Only 4/272 games had CUT>15%.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: D_positive (no failure: positive result)\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:BASE_RATE\n- observed_failure_evidence: Removing the 4 CUT-heavy games slightly strengthens the gap (+0.620 to +0.625).\n- observed_sample_and_power: 2,544 rows; 272 games\n- auto_validation_status: same_pipeline_validation; evidence: APPA-052: 'tale relative to n-gated +0.375 / best-vs-continue +0.445). robustness direction still holds on this csv. 2,544 rows; 272 game'\n- auto_related_family: FAM:SF32\n- observed_verdict: supported\n- auto_confidence: high (1.0)"}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPM-010", "score": 0.077, "document": "# FAM:SF-APPM-010 | Study family SF-APPM-010: Scheme-adjusted vs baseline Spearman across canonical series\n- observed_research_question: Scheme-adjusted vs baseline Spearman across canonical series\n- auto_outcome_status: supported\n- observed_hypothesis: Scheme-adjusted engine (Step 2) ranks play types better than baseline (Step 1).\n- observed_result: Mean Spearman +0.524 -> +0.579 (median +0.548 -> +0.631); improves 42/84, worsens 8/84, noise 34/84.\n- auto_failure_mechanism: D_positive (no failure: positive result)\n- auto_limited_by: LIM:small_sample\n- auto_has_risk: RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER\n- observed_failure_evidence: Mean delta +0.055; 42 improve vs 8 worse.\n- observed_sample_and_power: n=84 team rows; no test\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- observed_method: Per team-series Spearman for 84 team rows across canonical playoff slugs.\n- observed_verdict: supported\n- observed_failure_type: D_positive\n- observed_notes: Spearman target definition not stated in the file.\n- auto_confidence: high (0.95)"}], "n_results": 4}

Stage 2. Using the retrieval result above (follow-up tools are allowed within the tool budget), complete steps 4 to 9
and reply with the final action. Output schema (all fields required):
